29. Some of the Judgments relied on by the learned Special Government Pleader are apply to the instant cases and the same are as follows;
(i) In Nand Kishore Gupta's case (cited 9 supra), the Hon'ble Supreme Court held at para No.46 as under;
"The learned Counsel appearing on behalf of the appellants could not deny the fact that the total number of petitioners concerned in these acquisition proceedings,
coming up before the High Court, was extremely insignificant as compared to those who had accepted the compensation.
